LOK: a broken package's repair question is refused, not shown

BrokenPackageRequest fell back to the standard interaction handler,
which opens a modal dialog. In a headless LOK process nobody can
answer it, so the load never returned (Ely #49). Refuse the repair
and the notice like the other questions LOK answers itself: the
load fails with ERRCODE_IO_BROKENPACKAGE, and a "brokenpackage"
error callback tells the client why.
